00:33:06.238 --> 00:33:11.963
Uh, that is, uh, what we have seen,
like, on multiple, multiple of website.

00:33:11.997 --> 00:33:17.175
I would say roughly 70 to 80% websites
don't have a proper focus indicator.

00:33:17.759 --> 00:33:23.322
And that can be actually tackled, uh,
during the design phase, like I was

00:33:23.326 --> 00:33:25.271
also mentioning in, in the chat itself.

00:33:25.698 --> 00:33:31.005
Uh, if users are, you know… like if
developers or d- designers think about

00:33:31.008 --> 00:33:36.207
it at the very beginning, uh, this,
uh, chaos can be eliminated totally.

00:33:36.592 --> 00:33:42.639
Uh, but again, second, uh, in that
list would be, you know, predictability

00:33:42.640 --> 00:33:45.418
wherein focus jumps randomly to websites.

00:33:45.447 --> 00:33:50.028
Uh, like I've seen that in forms,
I've seen that in dialogues, and

00:33:50.036 --> 00:33:51.647
this is pretty common across…

00:33:51.919 --> 00:33:56.631
Again, I would put a random number out
